{
  "date": "2026-06-29",
  "title": "Who Are You Trying to Please?",
  "headline": "How to Stop Living for People’s Approval",
  "headline_sub": "Who Are You Trying to Please?",
  "tagline": "Every yes to approval is often a no to freedom.",
  "seo_title": "How to Stop Living for Approval: Galatians 1:10 for Men | TheWrkShop",
  "seo_description": "Fear of man is giving people authority over your identity. A devotional for men on Galatians 1:10 about approval, the crowd and the freedom of following Christ.",
  "keywords": [
    "people pleasing",
    "fear of man",
    "approval",
    "Galatians 1:10",
    "identity in Christ"
  ],
  "verse_ref": "Galatians 1:10",
  "verse_text": "For am I now seeking the approval of man, or of God? Or am I trying to please man? If I were still trying to please man, I would not be a servant of Christ.",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "Galatians 1:10",
      "text": "For am I now seeking the approval of man, or of God? Or am I trying to please man? If I were still trying to please man, I would not be a servant of Christ."
    },
    {
      "ref": "Joshua 24:15",
      "text": "Choose this day whom you will serve…."
    },
    {
      "ref": "John 14:6",
      "text": "I am the way, and the truth, and the life…."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "core_idea",
      "label": "Core Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Many men are unconsciously living for:",
            "approval,",
            "applause,",
            "acceptance,",
            "recognition,",
            "validation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Not because they consciously chose it.",
            "But because somewhere along the way they learned:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "acceptance feels safer than rejection."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "So they adapt.",
            "They perform.",
            "They manage perceptions.",
            "They become who others want them to be.",
            "And without realizing it….",
            "they slowly surrender their freedom."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "You cannot simultaneously follow the crowd and follow Christ when they move in opposite directions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "read_this_out_loud",
      "label": "Read This Out Loud",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The crowd is a terrible master.",
            "Because the crowd is never satisfied.",
            "If you live for approval….",
            "you will spend your life adjusting yourself to meet expectations that never stop changing.",
            "Freedom begins when God’s opinion becomes weightier than everyone else’s."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "moment_in_the_mirror",
      "label": "Moment in the Mirror",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Most men would never admit:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“I live for approval.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But many live as though they do."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "We see it in:",
            "the conversations we avoid,",
            "the truths we soften,",
            "the convictions we hide,",
            "the boundaries we abandon,",
            "the decisions we delay."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Because deep down we fear:",
            "being misunderstood,",
            "being rejected,",
            "disappointing people,",
            "losing acceptance,",
            "standing alone."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The result?",
            "We become loyal to the crowd."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_great_misunderstanding",
      "label": "The Great Misunderstanding",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Most men think fear of man is being afraid of people.",
            "But biblically it’s deeper.",
            "Fear of man is giving people authority over your identity."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "It happens whenever:",
            "their approval determines your peace.",
            "their criticism determines your confidence.",
            "their acceptance determines your decisions."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "At that point:",
            "they are no longer influencing you.",
            "They are ruling you."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "galatians_1_10",
      "label": "Galatians 1:10",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Paul draws a line in the sand.",
            "If pleasing people is your primary goal….",
            "serving Christ cannot remain your primary goal."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Notice he doesn’t say:",
            "“You can’t be kind.”",
            "“You can’t love people.”",
            "“You can’t listen to people.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "He says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "You cannot serve two masters."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Eventually every man chooses:",
            "Will I be governed by public opinion,",
            "or Kingdom conviction?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "joshua_24_15",
      "label": "Joshua 24:15",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Joshua stands before Israel and says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“Choose.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Not consider.",
            "Not explore.",
            "Not delay.",
            "Choose."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because allegiance always requires a decision."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Many men think neutrality exists.",
            "It doesn’t.",
            "Every day we are choosing:",
            "comfort or conviction,",
            "popularity or obedience,",
            "approval or freedom."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_part_most_men_miss",
      "label": "The Part Most Men Miss",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Jesus says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“I am the Way.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "He does not say the crowd is the way."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The crowd shifts constantly.",
            "Culture changes constantly.",
            "Opinions change constantly.",
            "Approval changes constantly.",
            "Jesus does not."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The crowd says “Fit in.” Jesus says “Follow Me.”",
            "The crowd says “Protect your image.” Jesus says “Lose your life.”",
            "The crowd says “Become acceptable.” Jesus says “Become faithful.”",
            "The crowd offers acceptance.",
            "Jesus offers freedom."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_approval_paradox",
      "label": "The Approval Paradox",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The more you need approval….",
            "the less free you become.",
            "The more you fear rejection….",
            "the more controlled you become.",
            "The more you seek validation….",
            "the more unstable your identity becomes."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Because approval is a moving target.",
            "Freedom begins when God’s approval becomes enough."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "root_check",
      "label": "Root Check",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Surface thought: “I don’t want to upset anyone.”",
            "Possible root: fear of rejection, criticism, disappointing people, standing alone.",
            "Deeper question: Whose opinion carries the most weight in my life?",
            "Core lie: “I need people’s approval to be okay.”",
            "Truth: God’s acceptance frees me from living for everyone else’s.",
            "Greater truth: Jesus is the Way. Not public opinion. Not culture. Not the crowd."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "gem_to_carry",
      "label": "Gem to Carry",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The crowd can applaud you and still lead you away from God."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
